{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the meaning of \"the angel who redeemed me,\" you will find in the section of Shemot." "<b>And let my name be called upon them.</b> For behold, all Israel are called Ephraim, also Joseph. Also, the verse said, \"Rachel weeping for her children\" (Jeremiah 31:15), for she was the principal object of his thought; therefore the verse said, \"the sons of Rachel, Jacob's wife\" (Genesis 46:19). And when Rachel gave birth, he immediately said to Laban, \"Send me away\" (Genesis 30:25). He also gave him the birthright, for he is the first of his thought. And after Reuben was not worthy of the birthright, Joseph was [worthy], for he is the firstborn of the womb — and not Dan or Gad, for they are sons of the maidservants. And the right [hand] is more honored than the left and more powerful."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:18.866942920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}